    <string name="nothing_yet">Nothing here yet.\n\nDescribe what you need below. Ephemeral records it — nothing is written or run until you generate it.</string>

    <!--
      Said on the first screen rather than buried in an about box. Somebody who
      taps "generate" and is left waiting for a build that will never happen has
      been misled by this app, not by the engine.

      This used to say a phone cannot run what it generates, full stop. That was
      true until it wasn't: a WebAssembly application runs here now (ADR-0021).
      A container one still cannot, and which of the two an application is is a
      property of the application — so the detail screen says it per application
      rather than making this sentence carry both.
    -->
    <string name="phone_limits">Generating writes the source to this phone. An application built for WebAssembly runs here too; one that needs a container is built and run on a computer.</string>

    <!-- What is true of one application, on the page for that application. -->
    <string name="runs_here">This one runs on your phone. It starts with no access to anything and reaches only what you allow.</string>
    <string name="needs_a_computer">This one needs a container, which a phone does not have. Its source is here; building and running it happen on a computer.</string>

